  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is the current best at 0.650 acc. We know avgpool beat transformer by ~7% with pca_n2000 (0.591 vs 0.519), but it is unclear whether this aggregation preference holds with the stronger scvi_n200 encoder. Question: config_006 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping scvi_n200 + multiprofile, directly isolating the aggregation effect under the best-known encoder. Why this is the best next step: it is a clean one-variable comparison against our current best, will definitively resolve whether transformer aggregation is ever useful in this pipeline, and the answer constrains all subsequent multimodal experiments (configs 032/033, 038/039, 044/045, 050/051 all hinge on this choice). If transformer is again worse, we can eliminate it and focus remaining budget on encoder (scgpt) and modality (multimodal) questions with confidence."
}

